@@ -20,6 +20,26 @@ All quiz data is in `storage/production.sqlite3` (including SQLite sidecar files
 
 Use a private/trusted network: HTTP Basic credentials are not encrypted over the intentionally plain-HTTP connection.
 
+## Run a live game
+
+Open a quiz in `/moderate` and press **Start a game**. Share its full join link
+or show the locally generated QR code. Each participant enters **Your name** and
+presses **Join**; no account is needed. Their browser remembers them for this game.
+
+Use **Start**, **Finish**, and **Next** to run the active questions, then **End
+quiz** after the last results. Phones and the big screen update live. Players can
+change a choice until Finish, and correct answers are never sent to players
+before that point. Joining mid-game is supported; joining after the end is not.
+
+Every game snapshots its active questions and keeps independent players/answers.
+The quiz page lists previous games so the moderator can reopen a running screen.
+All game state persists across server restarts. Use one Puma process (configured
+by default); no external pub/sub service is needed. If conference Wi-Fi blocks
+WebSockets, the client automatically falls back to HTTP updates.
+
+See [live-game design notes](docs/live-games.md) for presence counting,
+reconnection behavior, security boundaries, and concurrency/browser checks.
+
